# RULE 53 — SEED IN BULK, NEVER ROW BY ROW (owner 2026-09-28)

Owner, verbatim: **"all data must be seeded instantly and fast, not one by one."**

This is LAW for every seat, every backfill. It does not weaken Rule 52 (Faro purchase-day
composition / app writers only) or void-not-delete. When this rule and correct accounting
conflict, **accounting wins** — that is the only speed exception, and it is not a licence to be
slow anywhere else.

## THE RULE

Every seed, backfill, parse and correction is **SET-BASED** and runs in **ONE transaction per batch**.

Forbidden:

- Per-row HTTP call
- `for (const row of rows) await api.create(row)`
- A loop issuing one `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / engine call per record when a set-based write exists

That pattern is why a 300-row backfill takes an hour and why half of them land.

## HOW

1. **Parse the whole document into memory first**, validate the **WHOLE set**, then write.
2. **Set-based SQL:** `INSERT ... SELECT` · `UPDATE ... FROM (VALUES ...) AS v(...)` · `COPY`
   above a few thousand rows.
3. **One transaction per batch.** All-or-nothing. A partial seed is worse than no seed — nobody
   can tell which half is real.
4. **Batch 500–2000 rows.** Report **rows/second**.
5. **Validate BEFORE writing**, not per row during. If any row fails, the batch does not run and
   you report **EVERY** failing row at once — not the first one.

## THE ONE THING SPEED NEVER BUYS

Money still posts through the **sanctioned engine**. Do **NOT** hand-write journal entries or
postings to go faster. If the engine only exposes a per-document call, **batch the CALLS** — one
transaction, reused connection, stop re-reading the same catalog per row — but the posting logic
stays the engine's.

## WHERE THIS APPLIES RIGHT NOW (owner-named)

- **CC-2** — settlement lines `quantity` / `rate_cents` / `unit_of_measure`: remaining rows in ONE
  `UPDATE ... FROM (VALUES ...)`, not N updates. Same for settlements 5817 / 5818 / 5819.
- **CC-1** — unit / trailer / driver / customer / W.O. from the AlwaysTrack table — ONE statement.
  Mileage backfill across loads — ONE statement. Driver-bill re-mint — one batched transaction
  through the engine.
- **CC-3** — nothing to seed today; same law on any data migration shipped.
- **CURSOR** — match candidate pass over bank lines is **set-based**, not a loop over
  transactions. Faro **09-22..09-25** posts **one transaction per DAY**, not per invoice
  (Rule 52 composition still required; the day is the batch).

## PROOF

Every seed report states: **rows written · batches · seconds · rows/second · and that it ran in a
single transaction per batch.** A seed report without a rate is not a report.

## Guard

`scripts/verify-seed-in-bulk-never-row-by-row.mjs` — registered in `docs/law/LAW.json`. Fails if
this rule file is missing, stripped of its hard lines, or if new `scripts/ops/` seed/backfill
paths introduce an obvious per-row `await` create/insert loop without a set-based batch marker.
